## 1 Introduction
**Paper:** GradMem: Learning to Write Context into Memory · §1 · pages 1–2 · equations (1–1) · 1 figures.

**The baseline, stated precisely.** Conditioning on a context is concatenation
(eq. 1): the model sees `[C; Q]`. Everything else in the paper is an attempt to replace `C` in that bracket
with something much shorter without losing what the queries need.

